From 97c42489220d39e029568717686acf488c5ad56a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:41:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: measure item pickups from the nearest up staircase

borg_flow_take(), borg_flow_take_scum() and borg_flow_take_lunal() keep
a low-level borg's item hunts within a leash of its escape staircase.
Each looks up the nearest known up staircase for that test, but the scan
kept the farthest one instead ('skip the closer ones').

When the borg knew a second up staircase far away, an item a few steps
from the borg and from the staircase it was standing by was measured
against the distant staircase, judged too far from the stairs, and
ignored by all three pickup flows.

Keep the nearest up staircase in the three scans, matching their
comments and the 'closest stair' origin that borg_flow_spread() expects.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#71.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-take.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
index c5243ddd6..c00e5f6f3 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
@@ -471,8 +471,8 @@ bool borg_flow_take(bool viewable, int nearness)
         /* How far is the nearest up stairs */
         j = distance(borg.c, loc(x, y));
 
-        /* skip the closer ones */
-        if (b_j >= j)
+        /* skip the farther ones */
+        if (b_j <= j && b_j != -1)
             continue;
 
         /* track it */
@@ -620,8 +620,8 @@ bool borg_flow_take_scum(bool viewable, int nearness)
         /* How far is the nearest up stairs */
         j = distance(borg.c, loc(x, y));
 
-        /* skip the closer ones */
-        if (b_j >= j)
+        /* skip the farther ones */
+        if (b_j <= j && b_j != -1)
             continue;
 
         /* track it */
@@ -719,8 +719,8 @@ bool borg_flow_take_lunal(bool viewable, int nearness)
         /* How far is the nearest up stairs */
         j = distance(borg.c, loc(x, y));
 
-        /* skip the closer ones */
-        if (b_j >= j)
+        /* skip the farther ones */
+        if (b_j <= j && b_j != -1)
             continue;
 
         /* track it */
